rwtest 1
test "Drain leaves fed-on thoughts" project="Bernael" group="Soul" created=2026-09-18T00:00:00

# BX_SoulFeeding carries thoughtDefToGiveTarget BX_FedOn and
# opinionThoughtDefToGiveTarget BX_FedOn_Social. SoulUtility.DoDrain hands both
# to the victim's memories, the second one tagged with the biter.
#
# Nine of the ten ThoughtDefs in this mod had no test. These two are the ones
# that reach a pawn on the ability path; the rest hang on the prisoner jobs.
#
# Both memories go on the victim, not on the drainer - the social one is the
# victim's opinion of the drainer.
#
# BX_FedOn_Social carries baseOpinionOffset -20 and nothing else, and its
# presence is all this test reads. It used to bound the opinion as well, at
# -30..-10, and that line was wrong: opinion= is the whole relationship, not
# this thought's share of it.
#
# Vanilla's own situational social thoughts are in that sum and neither pawn is
# pinned against them. Disfigured alone is -15, and it applies whenever the
# drainer happens to carry a permanent scar or a missing part on an eye, ear,
# nose, jaw or tongue - which the pawn generator rolls - and vanishes entirely
# when the victim rolled Kind or Ascetic, because CaresAboutOthersAppearance is
# false for both. The line passed four runs and failed the fifth on the same
# assembly, reading -35: -20 from the mod, -15 from a roll.
#
# Both of those are pinned away now, and by "spawn" itself. Without rolled=true
# ShapePawn calls three things: GeneratedGear.StripFrom, GeneratedBody.ClearFrom
# and PawnTraits.Clear. ClearFrom puts missing body parts back and takes off
# every hediff that is a Hediff_MissingPart, chronic or permanent - exactly the
# three RelationsUtility.IsDisfigured reads. Clear takes every rolled trait,
# which puts Kind and Ascetic off the table as well.
#
# The line below does not read the sum at all any more. "assert opinion ... of=
# ... thought=" names this one thought's share of it, and that share is the
# def's own baseOpinionOffset: -20. The range is +/-5 around that single number
# and hangs on no chitchat, no trait and no scar.
#
# Until this kit only "opinion=" existed, and that is
# Pawn_RelationsTracker.OpinionOf - the whole relationship, vanilla's
# situational social thoughts included.
#
# If this number ever moves, the def changed and not the dice.

requires dlc=Biotech
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 0,0 name="Bernael" xenotype=BX_Bernael
spawn Pawn:Colonist at 1,0 name="Victim"

give "Bernael" resource=BX_SoulStarved value=0.1

# The drain goes through the "Soul drain" gizmo and a click on the victim, the
# player's route, so the 120-tick warmup runs before DoDrain. The waitfor holds
# that for at most 300 ticks; the memories land in the same Apply.
select "Bernael"
gizmo "Soul drain"
target "Victim"
waitfor pawn "Victim" thought=BX_FedOn expect=present ticks=300

assert pawn "Victim" thought=BX_FedOn expect=present
assert pawn "Victim" thought=BX_FedOn_Social expect=present
assert opinion "Victim" of="Bernael" thought=BX_FedOn_Social min=-25 max=-15
assert pawn "Victim" hediff=BX_SoulDrained expect=present
assert log clean
